# Downloaded dish photography, keyed by image_url. 40+ MB, and every byte of it
# is reproducible from Supabase on the next build — build_menu.py refills it.
_cache/

# render.sh's per-page temporaries. Namespaced by pid so two renders can run at
# once; they are deleted on a clean exit and left behind on a killed one.
_pg*
_shot*
_overflow-probe.html

# Generated. The HTML is the build's intermediate and the PDF is its output —
# both are rebuilt by `bash render.sh` from what IS tracked here.
menu-print*.html
sauce-sheet.html
*.pdf

# Written by build_menu.py as a by-product, for a human to sign off allergens.
allergen-review.tsv

# The repo root ignores *.png wholesale (line 80). photos/ is the one place that
# must not be: these are hand-composited artwork, not screenshots. The four
# rolls-*-x2.png each stage TWO rolls in one frame because the dish is sold as a
# pair, and no such image exists in Supabase — image_url points at a single
# roll. Lose these and the rows lose their photos with no way to rebuild them.
!photos/**/*.png
